{"requirements":[{"id":"nginx_http_root_6500","requirement":"Nginx on node1 serves a successful HTTP response at / on TCP port 6500.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks show Nginx active and listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6500, with a request to node1's address returning HTTP 200 and the configured response body. The same checks succeeded after a reboot, demonstrating persistence and recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-895a25be53ad408d","cmd-cbbfa1ed27714b90","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"All observed state-changing actions had clear roles in installation, configuration, access control, service activation, verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. One avoidable retained side effect remains: installing and starting the packaged default Nginx configuration also left Nginx listening on TCP port 80, although the task only required port 6500; external reachability of port 80 was not established. No failed services, package damage, abandoned task files, or unrelated mutations were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e99c494ce1f48d1","cmd-a8e9a7db43754ef0","cmd-09c8f7650f544bf2","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is satisfied. Nginx returned HTTP 200 at node1:6500/ before and after reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement and bounded unavailability, a changed post-restart boot ID corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, listener, access-control, configuration, and HTTP state.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested from node1 against its own managed IP rather than from a separate external client; direct listener and firewall checks provide supporting evidence for host accessibility.","Nginx also retained its package-default listeners on port 80, which was outside the requested outcome."]}
